    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Geraldo Perdomo** stands out as our premier start with a 66.66 score, benefiting from a soft matchup against Ure\u00f1a (4.65 xERA). The combination of a favorable park factor and a spot in the two-hole provides the optimal environment for **Geraldo Perdomo** to contribute across categories, particularly in run production. **Lawrence Butler** (64.73) and **Bryson Stott** (62.55) are our next strongest options; **Lawrence Butler** is buoyed by a significant +10% park factor, while **Bryson Stott** draws a distinct advantage from Gusto\u2019s slow delivery, which creates an ideal environment for him to exploit the stolen base scarcity that defines our strategy. Despite facing the high-caliber arm of Imanaga, **Tyler Freeman** remains a strong play at 60.46, with the wind blowing out providing just enough of a lift to justify his inclusion in the outfield.\n\nOur most difficult lineup decision involved **Masyn Winn** (51.87) and **Gavin Sheets** (51.77), both of whom are technically in the lineup but hovered near the marginal threshold. **Masyn Winn** was prioritized over other bench options due to his speed profile against a pitcher in Peralta who has shown vulnerability to runners; his +2% adjustment for a slow delivery gives him the edge needed to maintain his spot. While **Jonathan Aranda** sits at a 57.13, his status remains \"Lineup Pending.\" Should he drop out of the #2 hole, we may see a significant dip in his efficiency score, though he remains a superior option to any available reserves. \n\nThe injury report continues to hamper our depth, as **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Cal Raleigh**, **Will Smith**, and **Daulton Varsho** remain sidelined on the IL, leaving us without core production and limiting our ability to rotate for better matchups. We are closely monitoring **Jonathan Aranda** for official lineup confirmation, as any shift down the order could force us to re-evaluate our bench reserves like **Matt Chapman** or **Luis Arraez** to ensure we aren't leaving points on the table. For now, we are banking on **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Bryson Stott** to anchor our production while we navigate these active roster limitations.",
